// coop_world.cpp -- store A (world booleans), the store-A ledger, lifts, chests.
//
// Ported from G:\Freespace\shell_coop\ms2-coop\mod\CoopMod\Scripts\main.lua:
//   2197-2602  wsHash/wsBool/wsValid/wsMarkTrue, WSL.*, wsScan, wsBuildPayload,
//              wsReadPeer, wsOwnerActor, wsApplyOne, wsApply, wsJudge, wsTick,
//              wsTest, wsStatus
//   3344-3496  LF.*, liftReadPeer, liftTest, liftTick, liftStatus
//   3497-3737  CS.*, csReadPeer, CS.grant, CS.judge, csTest, chestTick,
//              chestStatus
//
// Behaviour, log text, wire bytes, rates, budgets and settle windows are the
// Lua's, bug-for-bug. Two things about this subsystem are load-bearing and are
// explained where they are implemented:
//
//   * SpartaSaveSubSystem.SaveObjects (TMap<FGuid, ...>) HARD-CRASHES the game
//     when iterated (HANDOFF.md 14 / HANDOFF-REMAINING-SYNC.md 176). Nothing in
//     this file touches it. The Lua does not use it either: it keys every save
//     object by a hash of its owning actor's name, and keeps a text ledger of
//     the keys it has ever known true so state survives an actor streaming out.
//   * a value is not trusted until its object has existed for kWsSettle (8 s):
//     a freshly loaded BP_HubDoor_C reads DoorIsOpen=true for ~3 s until its
//     save is applied. Ignoring that gate makes both clients flap.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CONTRACT-REQUESTs (things coop_state.h / ms2_ue.h cannot express)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. net::ReadText(name, out): the store-A ledger is one 8-hex key per line, so
//    the single-line net::ReadLine() cannot load it. Declared below; it must
//    read the whole file, return false when the file does not exist.
// 2. A way to free a TArray that a UFunction returned by value into the Parms
//    block (ue::FreeTArray(void* data) or similar). USpartaItemManagerComponent
//    ::GetAllItems() returns TArray<USpartaItemInstance*> that the callee
//    allocated; nothing releases it. This file deliberately LEAKS it (freeing
//    with a mismatched allocator is a crash) -- roughly one array of a few
//    hundred pointers per 500 ms while the chest snapshot runs.
// 3. WsRow::v is tri-state in the Lua: nil until the object is kWsSettle old,
//    and `e.v == false` (the apply / local-flip / wsTest precondition) is FALSE
//    for a nil row. WsRow has only `bool v`, so the third state lives in a
//    private index-aligned vector (gRowKnown) in this file. A `bool hasV` field
//    would make it explicit; nothing else reads/writes row.v.
// 4. LedgerState has no `n` (the Lua's WSL.n): keys.Size() is used, which is the
//    same number because `n` only counts WSL.keys.
// 5. LedgerState has no `applied` table (the Lua's WSL.applied: key -> row used
//    by the result_ledger.txt verdict). Kept privately here as a vector of keys.
// 6. ue::GetName(o) must equal UE4SS's `o:GetFName():ToString()`: the lift and
//    chest wire names are that string, compared verbatim by the other client.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Engine facts this file relies on (verified in
// research/raw/Dumper7_*/.../CppSDK/SDK, UE 5.6.1 build CL92086):
//   * every store-A flag (DoorIsOpen, MyBool, ItemCollected, Unlocked, ...) and
//     BP_HubLift_C.bLiftActive are plain 1-byte `bool` (IsPlainOldData), NOT
//     packed bitfields, so a byte read/write is exact;
//   * BP_HubLift_C.TargetFloor and BP_Interactable_Chest_C.TimesUsed are int32;
//   * BP_HubLift_C.SM_Lift is a UStaticMeshComponent, BP_Interactable_Chest_C
//     .SK_Chest a USkeletalMeshComponent, .ChestMontage a UAnimSequence;
//   * USpartaSaveObject::GetOwningActor() is the owner of a store-A object;
//   * UFunction parameter names used here (GetComponentByClass.ComponentClass,
//     GetAllItems.ReturnValue, GetTotalItemCountByDefinition.ItemDef,
//     AddItemByClass.ItemDef/StackCount, PlayAnimation.NewAnimToPlay/bLooping,
//     SetPosition.InPos/bFireNotifies, GetPosition.ReturnValue,
//     SetActorHiddenInGame.bNewHidden, SetActorEnableCollision
//     .bNewActorEnableCollision, SpartaWorldStateHelper.WriteAnInt
//     .WorldContextObject/OwnerName/ValueName/Value/bModify) are the SDK's.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <cstring>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

#include "ms2_ue.h"
